  "request": {
    "model": "nomic-embed-text:latest",
    "input": [
      "Synthetic nurse note for software testing. No real patient data.\n\nIn a commercial-driver follow-up arranged after an occupational screening concern, the nurse interviews the driver and checks the accompanying documents against the reported sequence of events; the employer wants a quick answer before allocating a vehicle, but the record separates present evidence, historical findings and questions that the clinician has not yet resolved.\n\nA colleague witnessed the driver lose consciousness and fail to respond for 25 seconds during a break, and the current physician referral explicitly records a blackout with the mechanism under investigation; although the driver recalls heat, hunger and a racing heartbeat beforehand, neither syncope, seizure nor hypoglycaemia has been confirmed, cardiac monitoring is pending, and uncertainty about a remote dizzy spell does not erase the documented recent event.\n\nThe usual work involves coupling trailers, checking mirrors, interpreting radio messages and responding to pedestrians in a loading area, with breaks that can be delayed when deliveries run late; the driver explains which difficulty occurred while stationary and which was noticed during ordinary duties, rather than claiming that quiet conversation in the clinic reproduces every task in the cab.\n\nBefore closing the interview, the nurse checks that the driver's recollection and the supplied clinical document have not been merged into a single undated finding, and records the outstanding documents separately; the completed entries remain current findings, while any missing qualification, conflicting detail or unperformed examination stays available for review rather than being silently treated as normal.\n"
    ],
    "truncate": false
  },
  "provider_called": true,
  "status": "completed",
